# LINE ENDINGS — the general rule first, the byte-identity pins after.
#
# Ordering matters: git applies the LAST matching pattern, so the `-text` pins
# at the bottom override the blanket rule for the paths whose bytes ARE their
# identity.
#
# Why a blanket rule at all: with no attribute, the line-ending form of every
# checked-out file is inherited from the cloning host's git config. Git for
# Windows, including the GitHub-hosted windows-2025 runner image that runs the
# windows-amd64 coverage target, installs with core.autocrlf=true and rewrites
# LF to CRLF at checkout. `* text=auto eol=lf` makes the working-tree bytes a
# property of the repository instead of the host, and normalizes a CRLF edit
# back to LF at commit. `text=auto` uses git's NUL-byte heuristic, so binaries
# are left alone.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14 with `git ls-files --eol`: all 403 tracked blobs are
# i/lf or i/none, with zero i/crlf, i/mixed, or binary blobs, so this file
# changes no byte of the current tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTE-IDENTITY PINS — these MUST stay below the blanket rule to take effect.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GENERATED OOD GRAPH SCHEMA: THE BYTES ARE BOUND BY SHA-256 IN THE RECEIPT.
#
# bootstrap/schema_ood_graph_protocol_v1.render-receipt.json carries
# rendered_ddl_sha256, and oodschema.VerifyRendered recomputes that digest over
# the exact bytes of the generated .sql. On PR #79 the windows-amd64 target
# failed TestGeneratedOODGraphSchemaMatchesReceipt with "rendered DDL SHA-256
# does not match its receipt" because the runner's core.autocrlf=true checkout
# had rewritten the .sql to CRLF. Reproduced locally by cloning with
# `git -c core.autocrlf=true clone` (w/crlf, test FAIL) before this file existed.
#
# `-text`, not `text eol=lf`: -text tells git these blobs are never translated
# in EITHER direction, so the committed bytes are the working-tree bytes on
# every platform. The renderer owns their line endings, not git.
bootstrap/*.generated.sql -text
bootstrap/*.render-receipt.json -text
